# text = The old gentleman stopped , laid down his pen , and looked from Oliver to Mr . Limbkins ; who attempted to take snuff with a cheerful and unconcerned aspect said the old gentleman said the other magistrate : laying aside the paper , and leaning forward with an expression of interest Oliver fell on his knees , and clasping his hands together , prayed that they would order him back to the dark room -- that they would starve him -- beat him -- kill him if they pleased -- rather than send him away with that dreadful man said Mr . Bumble , raising his hands and eyes with most impressive solemnity said the second old gentleman , when Mr . Bumble had given vent to this compound adjective said Mr . Bumble , incredulous of having heard aright Mr . Bumble was stupefied with astonishment .
