# text = But they made no reply said the Jew , seizing the Dodger tightly by the collar , and threatening him with horrid imprecations Mr . Fagin looked so very much in earnest , that Charley Bates , who deemed it prudent in all cases to be on the safe side , and who conceived it by no means improbable that it might be his turn to be throttled second , dropped upon his knees , and raised a loud , well-sustained , and continuous roar -- something between a mad bull and a speaking trumpet thundered the Jew : shaking the Dodger so much that his keeping in the big coat at all , seemed perfectly miraculous said the Dodger , sullenly
