# text = It is worthy of remark , as illustrating the importance we attach to our own judgments , and the pride with which we put forth our most rash and hasty conclusions , that , although Mr . Grimwig was not by any means a bad-hearted man , and though he would have been unfeignedly sorry to see his respected friend duped and deceived , he really did most earnestly and strongly hope at that moment , that Oliver Twist might not come back .
