# text = A dog growled as he touched the handle of a room-door ; and a man's voice demanded who was there said the Jew looking in said Sikes Apparently , the dog had been somewhat deceived by Mr . Fagin's outer garment ; for as the Jew unbuttoned it , and threw it over the back of a chair , he retired to the corner from which he had risen : wagging his tail as he went , to show that he was as well satisfied as it was in his nature to be said Sikes replied the Jew The latter recognition was uttered with just enough of embarrassment to imply a doubt of its reception ; for Mr . Fagin and his young friend had not met , since she had interfered in behalf of Oliver .
