# text = At first , he was pleased with the discovery : hoping that it might be the forerunner of his release ; but such thoughts were quickly dispelled , on his sitting down to breakfast along with the Jew , who told him , in a tone and manner which increased his alarm , that he was to be taken to the residence of Bill Sikes that night asked Oliver , anxiously replied the Jew The old man , who was stooping over the fire toasting a piece of bread , looked round as he bantered Oliver thus ; and chuckled as if to show that he knew he would still be very glad to get away if he could said the Jew , fixing his eyes on Oliver Oliver coloured , involuntarily , to find that the old thief had been reading his thoughts ; but boldly said , Yes , he did want to know inquired Fagin , parrying the question replied Oliver said the Jew , turning away with a disappointed countenance from a close perusal of the boy's face The Jew seemed much vexed by Oliver's not expressing any greater curiosity on the subject ; but the truth is , that , although Oliver felt very anxious , he was too much confused by the earnest cunning of Fagin's looks , and his own speculations , to make any further inquiries just then .
