# text = It is a common thing for the countenances of the dead , even in that fixed and rigid state , to subside into the long-forgotten expression of sleeping infancy , and settle into the very look of early life ; so calm , so peaceful , do they grow again , that those who knew them in their happy childhood , kneel by the coffin's side in awe , and see the Angel even upon earth .
