# text = Mr . Bumble , who was ashamed or afraid to lag behind , followed : obviously very ill at ease and with scarcely any of that remarkable dignity which was usually his chief characteristic said Monks , turning round , and addressing Bumble , after he had bolted the door behind them stammered Bumble , looking apprehensively about him retorted Monks With this agreeable speech , Monks turned short upon the matron , and bent his gaze upon her , till even she , who was not easily cowed , was fain to withdraw her eyes , and turn them towards the ground demanded Monks replied Mr . Bumble , mindful of his wife's caution said the matron , interposing , and returning , as she spoke , the searching look of Monks said Monks asked the matron replied Monks rejoined the matron , slightly colouring as she spoke said Monks Bestowing something half-way between a smile and a frown upon his two companions , and again beckoning them to follow him , the man hastened across the apartment , which was of considerable extent , but low in the roof .
