# text = In compliance with Mr . Fagin's request , the Artful untied this bundle , which was of large size , and formed of an old table-cloth ; and handed the articles it contained , one by one , to Charley Bates : who placed them on the table , with various encomiums on their rarity and excellence exclaimed that young gentleman , disclosing to view a huge pasty Uttering this last panegyric , Master Bates produced , from one of his extensive pockets , a full-sized wine-bottle , carefully corked ; while Mr . Dawkins , at the same instant , poured out a wine-glassful of raw spirits from the bottle he carried : which the invalid tossed down his throat without a moment's hesitation said Fagin , rubbing his hands with great satisfaction exclaimed Mr . Sikes said Fagin , shrugging his shoulders observed Mr . Sikes : a little soothed as he glanced over the table cried Master Bates , doing as he was desired cried Sikes , as the dog retreated under the bed : still growling angrily replied the Jew demanded Sikes growled Sikes , with excessive disgust urged Fagin , submissively replied Sikes , with a bitter grin remonstrated Fagin , eagerly catching at the word said Nancy , coming hastily forward Nancy's appearance gave a new turn to the conversation ; for the boys , receiving a sly wink from the wary old Jew , began to ply her with liquor : of which , however , she took very sparingly ; while Fagin , assuming an unusual flow of spirits , gradually brought Mr . Sikes into a better temper , by affecting to regard his threats as a little pleasant banter ; and , moreover , by laughing very heartily at one or two rough jokes , which , after repeated applications to the spirit-bottle , he condescended to make said Mr .
# sent_id = 2228
