# text = Thus , they had toiled along the dusty road , taking little heed of any object within sight , save when they stepped aside to allow a wider passage for the mail-coaches which were whirling out of town , until they passed through Highgate archway ; when the foremost traveller stopped and called impatiently to his companion said the female , coming up , almost breathless with fatigue rejoined the male traveller , changing his own little bundle as he spoke , to the other shoulder asked the woman , resting herself against a bank , and looking up with the perspiration streaming from her face said the long-legged tramper , pointing out before him said the woman despondingly said Noah Claypole ; for he it was As Noah's red nose grew redder with anger , and as he crossed the road while speaking , as if fully prepared to put his threat into execution , the woman rose without any further remark , and trudged onward by his side she asked , after they had walked a few hundred yards replied Noah , whose temper had been considerably impaired by walking said Charlotte replied Mr . Claypole replied Mr . Claypole with dignity said his companion said Mr . Claypole in a jeering tone . ' No !
