# text = I would paint her the life and joy of the fire-side circle and the lively summer group ; I would follow her through the sultry fields at noon , and hear the low tones of her sweet voice in the moonlit evening walk ; I would watch her in all her goodness and charity abroad , and the smiling untiring discharge of domestic duties at home ; I would paint her and her dead sister's child happy in their love for one another , and passing whole hours together in picturing the friends whom they had so sadly lost ; I would summon before me , once again , those joyous little faces that clustered round her knee , and listen to their merry prattle ; I would recall the tones of that clear laugh , and conjure up the sympathising tear that glistened in the soft blue eye .
